<div style="padding: 50px; width: 700px;">
  <h1>Example snippet (Syncify demo)</h1>

  <h2>This is added in theme.liquid layout</h2>
  <p>

    This file is contained within a snippets sub-directory, but will be output to your
    themes snippets directory. This file will also be HOT Reloaded, even though it is
    a snippet which contains Liquid.

    {% assign foo = 'something' %}

    {% if foo == 'something' %}

    {% capture text %}

      <h3>Testing Capture</h3>
      <p style="width: 400px">
        The Shopify CLI has a dozen "engineers" working on it who get paid
        thousands of dollars per month to develop/improve it and yet despite that,
        it does not support snippet HOT reloading. Why? because Shopify engineers
        are not very good. However, Syncify supports this feature!
      </p>
      <p>
        Edit this file in HOT mode and see the changes in real time!
      </p>
    {% endcapture %}

    {{ text }}

    {% endif %}

  </p>
</div>